  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Grovre/Buffering",
  "published": "2026-08-22T01:30:55.347Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Buffering 1.0.0 Release Notes:\n- Redesigned architecture to a high-performance, lock-free Single-Writer Multiple-Reader (SWMR) concurrency model.\n- Eliminated locking overhead and contention using full memory barriers (Interlocked.MemoryBarrier).\n- Removed wrapper allocations (StrongBox<T>) and lock objects for zero-allocation buffer operations and instant construction.\n- Introduced decoupled, lightweight handle types: DoubleBufferFrontReader<T> and DoubleBufferBackWriter<T>.\n- Configurable swap effects via DoubleBufferSwapEffect (FlipRefOrValue for zero-allocation recycling; CopyRefOrValue for persistent baseline state).\n- Built-in pending update detection to avoid redundant swap operations.\n- Full Native AOT and Trimming support on .NET 10.0+.",
